  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066378/assets/2b5d589462bf2477be3d305ea88f3d5462b7d6ea4e001a9a71790d53e1683665.png)\n\nThe area of the square above is increasing. The length of the side of the square is $l.$ Find the rate of change of the area of a square with respect to the length of its side.",
  "worked_solution": "The area of the square is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(l)={l}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length of the side of the square.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(l)$ with respect to $l$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{\u2032}(l) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}l}({l}^{2})=2l.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
